meta {
  name: Request Mobile Verification
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/account/request-mobile-verification
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "mobile": "09120000002"
  }
}

docs {
  ## Purpose

  Issue a verification code for a new mobile number for the current account.

  ## Authentication

  Requires a valid access token.

  ## Behavior

  - The new number must differ from the current one and match the supported mobile format.
  - Complete the change in the same session with `PATCH /account/update-profile`, sending the same `mobile` and the issued `otp`.
  - Local development uses a configured code; production delivery is not implemented.
  - A cooldown and a bounded in-process attempt limit apply.

  ## Response

  - `200 OK` — Verification code issued.
  - `400 Bad Request` — The number is invalid or unchanged.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — Authentication is required.
  - `429 Too Many Requests` — The cooldown or attempt limit applies.
}
